ard  problems to solve before getting to that  proverbial one dot oh can you give us a  sense of like what's the big thorny  issues on your mind performance is an  issue we need to make sure that that  people understand exactly how much  latency will this add how much more  compute is it gonna add we've got the  API is pretty stable right now we need  to make sure it is stable at scale  although we do have you know whether  comm is running it about 400,000  requests a second so we were already  getting into pretty good production  stability there I was gonna ask you  about scale actually you you jumped one  step ahead of me here but four hundred  thousand containers all right sorry four  hundred thousand requests per second is  outstanding does this do help does this  do help stave off some of those some of  the  work that someone might have to do  otherwise without a service mesh in  place to help with that sort of  scalability of traffic what it does to  your to your scalability of traffic it  allows you to understand your system  better today too many people are scaling  pods on things like memory consumption  or CPU when in reality what you might  want to scale on is the amount of  traffic that you're getting or what your  latency czar doing and so it's actually  giving better tools to your operators to  to be able to run those systems better  gotcha so earlier today we've we've just  heard about the stack driver  announcements can you tell us about how  sto and stack driver might interact well  we already have in open source a a mixer  plug-in mixers one of the components of  sto that gathers telemetry a plug-in  today that that will send all of your  sto telemetry to stackdriver  we've got some really interesting things  and it works with that team right now  some stuff that we can't talk about but  you know they they announced this  kubernetes thing we're already working  on on the next big thing with those guys  okay last question security is on  everyone's 